  "recordType": "rule-part",
  "ruleText": "Part Ins 6202 had been based on the former rules Ins 1901.05(e), Ins 1901.06(e), and Ins 1901.07(a)(14) and (17). The former Ins 1901.06 and Ins 1901.07 had been titled as noted in Revision Note #1 above, and had expired 4-17-14. The former Ins 1901.05 had been titled “Prohibited Policy Provisions” and had also expired 4-17-14. Part Ins 6202 replaces the provisions cited above in the former Ins 1901.05, Ins 1901.06, and Ins 1901.07.\n\nThe filings affecting the former Ins 1901.06 and Ins 1901.07 included the documents cited in Revision Note #1 above. The filings affecting the former Ins 1901.05 included the following documents:\n\n#1900, effective 1-1-82\n\n#4287, effective 7-1-87\n\n#4811, effective 5-4-90\n\n#5656, effective 7-1-93\n\n#5943, effective 1-1-95 (Ins 1901.05(e) EXPIRED 1-1-03)\n\n#7017, INTERIM, effective 7-1-99, EXPIRED 10-29-99\n\n#8609, effective 4-17-06, EXPIRED 4-17-14\n\nREVISION NOTE #3:\n\nDocument #12855, effective 8-26-19, adopted Part Ins 6203 titled “Ancillary Health Minimum Standards for Accident-Only and Specified Accident Coverage.”",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins6200.html"
